-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- LAYER 1, part ssc6: Part 12ZB, Statutory Adoption Pay (ss 171ZL-171ZT).
-- Lines 3559-3717 of ukpga-1992-4.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is "verified against the official text".
--
-- How to read a result (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed and not ruled by a lawyer):
--   JUST FALSE answers "the text says no in its own words" and carries a comment
--       -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the quoted words>"
--   NOTHING answers "not covered" and carries a comment  -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Money is a NUMBER in pounds sterling; a figure is weekly unless its name says otherwise.
-- Numbers that regulations supply ("prescribed") are inputs. Numbers the Act states in its own words
-- (26 weeks, 28 days, 52 weeks, 6 weeks, 90 per cent) are constants.
-- The converter shows "..." or a line of dots where words or a limb were repealed (src:3578, 3616, 3685, 3686).
-- The surviving words are encoded; the dots are not.

§ `Part 12ZB -- Statutory Adoption Pay`

-- Helper (it implements no provision): the three-valued AND of a list of answers.
-- JUST FALSE if any answer is JUST FALSE; JUST TRUE if every answer is JUST TRUE; NOTHING otherwise.
-- The JUST FALSE it returns is the "no" of the calling rule, whose own comment quotes the text.
GIVEN answers IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(1) all of these answers hold` MEANS
    CONSIDER answers
    WHEN EMPTY THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER first
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `s 171ZL(1) all of these answers hold` rest
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            CONSIDER `s 171ZL(1) all of these answers hold` rest
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `s 171ZL Entitlement`

-- The Act's own numbers: weeks of continuous employment, and days of notice.
-- src:3564 | (b) that he has been in employed earner’s employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least 26 weeks ending with the relevant week;
@ref s 171ZL(2)(b) (src:3564)
`s 171ZL(2)(b) the number of weeks of continuous employment required` MEANS 26

-- src:3583 | (b) the notice is given at least 28 days before that date or, if that is not reasonably practicable, as soon as is reasonably practicable.
@ref s 171ZL(6)(b) (src:3583)
`s 171ZL(6)(b) the least number of days of notice before the liability begins` MEANS 28

-- Plain gloss: the conditions a person must meet to be entitled to statutory adoption pay.
-- (a) A child is, or is expected to be, placed with him for adoption in the United Kingdom.
-- src:3563 | (a) that he is a person with whom a child is, or is expected to be, placed for adoption under the law of any part of the United Kingdom;
@ref s 171ZL(2)(a) (src:3563)
GIVEN `he is a person with whom a child is, or is expected to be, placed for adoption under the law of any part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(2)(a) he is a person with whom a child is, or is expected to be, placed for adoption` MEANS
    IF `he is a person with whom a child is, or is expected to be, placed for adoption under the law of any part of the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are— (a) that he is a person with whom a child is, or is expected to be, placed for adoption under the law of any part of the United Kingdom"

-- Plain gloss: (b) he has worked for an employer for at least 26 weeks running up to the "relevant
-- week" (the week he is told he has been matched with the child).
-- src:3564 | (b) that he has been in employed earner’s employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least 26 weeks ending with the relevant week;
@ref s 171ZL(2)(b) (src:3564)
GIVEN service IS A `Service for statutory pay`
      `his employment with the employer is employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(2)(b) he has been in employed earner's employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least 26 weeks ending with the relevant week` MEANS
    IF     `his employment with the employer is employed earner's employment`
       AND service's `weeks of continuous employment with the employer ending with the relevant week`
               AT LEAST `s 171ZL(2)(b) the number of weeks of continuous employment required`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are—"

-- Plain gloss: (c) he has stopped working for that employer.
-- src:3565 | (c) that he has ceased to work for the employer;
@ref s 171ZL(2)(c) (src:3565)
GIVEN `he has ceased to work for the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(2)(c) he has ceased to work for the employer` MEANS
    IF `he has ceased to work for the employer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are—"

-- Plain gloss: (d) over the 8 weeks up to the relevant week he earned, on average, at least the lower
-- earnings limit in force at the end of the relevant week (a figure regulations set, so the caller supplies it).
-- src:3566 | (d) that his normal weekly earnings for the period of 8 weeks ending with the relevant week are not less than the lower earnings limit in force under section 5(1)(a) at the end of the relevant week; and
@ref s 171ZL(2)(d) (src:3566)
GIVEN service IS A `Service for statutory pay`
      `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(2)(d) his normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit at the end of the relevant week` MEANS
    IF service's `normal weekly earnings in pounds over the period the section names`
           AT LEAST `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are—"

-- Plain gloss: (e) he has elected to receive statutory adoption pay.
-- src:3567 | (e) that he has elected to receive statutory adoption pay.
@ref s 171ZL(2)(e) (src:3567)
GIVEN `he has elected to receive statutory adoption pay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(2)(e) he has elected to receive statutory adoption pay` MEANS
    IF `he has elected to receive statutory adoption pay`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are—"

-- src:3562 | (2) The conditions are—
@ref s 171ZL(2) (src:3562)
GIVEN `condition (a) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `condition (b) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `condition (c) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `condition (d) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `condition (e) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(2) the conditions are satisfied` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are—"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb that depends on a figure or fact regulations supply is NOTHING when the caller does not supply it
    `s 171ZL(1) all of these answers hold` (LIST `condition (a) is satisfied`, `condition (b) is satisfied`, `condition (c) is satisfied`, `condition (d) is satisfied`, `condition (e) is satisfied`)

-- Plain gloss: a person who is, or has been, an employee and meets the conditions is entitled to
-- payments "in accordance with the following provisions of this Part": notice (subsection (6)),
-- the weeks (s 171ZN) and the other bars still apply.
-- src:3561 | (1) Where a person who is, or has been, an employee satisfies the conditions in subsection (2) below, he shall be entitled in accordance with the following provisions of this Part to payments to be known as “statutory adoption pay”.
@ref s 171ZL(1) (src:3561)
GIVEN `s 171ZS(2) the person is, or has been, an employee` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 171ZL(2) the conditions are satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(1) he is entitled to statutory adoption pay` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person who is, or has been, an employee satisfies the conditions in subsection (2) below, he shall be entitled" (marginal reading (a): a failed "where" counts as the text's no)
    `s 171ZL(1) all of these answers hold` (LIST `s 171ZS(2) the person is, or has been, an employee`, `s 171ZL(2) the conditions are satisfied`)

-- Plain gloss: the "relevant week" in (2)(b) and (d) is the week in which he is told he has been
-- matched with the child (for a placement under s 22C or s 81, the week in which he is told the
-- child is to be, or is expected to be, placed with him). A Sunday-to-Saturday week unless
-- regulations prescribe another. This is the answer ssc7's s 171ZZ16 asks for (seam S30).
-- src:3568 | (3) The references in subsection (2)(b) and (d) above to the relevant week are to the week in which the person is notified that he has been matched with the child for the purposes of adoption.
-- src:3601 | (b) the reference in subsection (3) to the week in which the person is notified that he has been matched with the child for the purposes of adoption is to be treated as a reference to the week in which the person is notified that the child is to be, or is expected to be, placed with him under section 22C;
-- src:3607 | (b) the reference in subsection (3) to the week in which the person is notified that he has been matched with the child for the purposes of adoption is to be treated as a reference to the week in which the person is notified that the child is to be, or is expected to be placed with him under section 8;
@ref s 171ZL(3), s 171ZL(9)(b), s 171ZL(11)(b) (src:3568) (src:3601) (src:3607)
GIVEN placement IS A Placement
      `regulations prescribe another period in place of a week beginning with Sunday for the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
`s 171ZL(2) the relevant week` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 171ZS(5) the first day of the week containing the day` (placement's `the day the person was notified of the match`) `regulations prescribe another period in place of a week beginning with Sunday for the case`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the week is the one "as may be prescribed"
    WHEN JUST notifiedWeek THEN
        JUST (Period WITH
                  `the first day` IS notifiedWeek
                  `the last day` IS notifiedWeek PLUS 6)

-- Plain gloss: the three couple-law cases of subsection (4B).
DECLARE `s 171ZL(4B) Law of adoption` IS ONE OF
    `s 171ZL(4B) the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland`
    `s 171ZL(4B) the law of Scotland`
    `s 171ZL(4B) the law of another place`

-- Plain gloss: whether a person is a member of a couple, for the purposes of the bar in
-- subsection (4A). Which test applies depends on the law the adoption is under: in England and
-- Wales or Northern Ireland, section 144(4) of the Adoption and Children Act 2002; in Scotland,
-- section 29(3) of the Adoption and Children (Scotland) Act 2007. Neither Act is among the
-- sources, so each answer is asked as a fact. The limb between them is blank in the text (src:3578).
-- For a placement under s 22C or s 81, subsections (9)(c) and (11)(c) read "adoption" in limb (a)
-- as that placement, so the caller picks the England and Wales or Northern Ireland case for it.
-- src:3576 | (4B) For the purposes of subsection (4A), a person is a member of a couple if—
-- src:3577 | (a) in the case of an adoption or expected adoption under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland, he is a member of a couple within the meaning of section 144(4) of the Adoption and Children Act 2002;
-- src:3579 | (c) in the case of an adoption or expected adoption under the law of Scotland he is a member of a relevant couple within the meaning of section 29(3) of the Adoption and Children (Scotland) Act 2007.
-- src:3602 | (c) the references in subsection (4B)(a) to adoption are to be treated as references to placement under section 22C;
-- src:3608 | (c) the references in subsection (4B)(a) to adoption are to be treated as references to placement under section 81;
@ref s 171ZL(4B), s 171ZL(9)(c), s 171ZL(11)(c) (src:3576-3577) (src:3579) (src:3602) (src:3608)
GIVEN law IS A `s 171ZL(4B) Law of adoption`
      `he is a member of a couple within the meaning of section 144(4) of the Adoption and Children Act 2002` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `he is a member of a relevant couple within the meaning of section 29(3) of the Adoption and Children (Scotland) Act 2007` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(4B) he is a member of a couple` MEANS
    CONSIDER law
    WHEN `s 171ZL(4B) the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland` THEN `he is a member of a couple within the meaning of section 144(4) of the Adoption and Children Act 2002`        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 144(4) of the 2002 Act is not among the sources
    WHEN `s 171ZL(4B) the law of Scotland` THEN `he is a member of a relevant couple within the meaning of section 29(3) of the Adoption and Children (Scotland) Act 2007`        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 29(3) of the 2007 Act is not among the sources
    WHEN `s 171ZL(4B) the law of another place` THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names three cases, one of them blank in this text, and no other

-- Plain gloss: he falls within the bar of (4A) if the child is, or is expected to be, placed with him
-- as a member of a couple, the other member meets the conditions of subsection (2), and the other
-- member has elected to receive statutory adoption pay. A definition by "if" is read as closed
-- (marginal reading (a)).
-- src:3572 | (4A) A person falls within this subsection if—
-- src:3573 | (a) the child is, or is expected to be, placed for adoption with him as a member of a couple;
-- src:3574 | (b) the other member of the couple is a person to whom the conditions in subsection (2) above apply; and
-- src:3575 | (c) the other member of the couple has elected to receive statutory adoption pay.
@ref s 171ZL(4A) (src:3572-3575)
GIVEN `the child is, or is expected to be, placed for adoption with him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 171ZL(4B) he is a member of a couple` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the other member of the couple is a person to whom the conditions in subsection (2) apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other member of the couple has elected to receive statutory adoption pay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(4A) he falls within the subsection` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person falls within this subsection if—" (marginal reading (a): a failed "if" counts as the text's no)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether he is a member of a couple is subsection (4B)'s answer
    `s 171ZL(1) all of these answers hold`
        (LIST (IF `the child is, or is expected to be, placed for adoption with him` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE),
              `s 171ZL(4B) he is a member of a couple`,
              (IF `the other member of the couple is a person to whom the conditions in subsection (2) apply` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE),
              (IF `the other member of the couple has elected to receive statutory adoption pay` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE))

-- Plain gloss: he may not elect to receive statutory adoption pay if he has elected, under s 171ZB,
-- to receive statutory paternity pay, or if he falls within (4A).
-- src:3569 | (4) A person may not elect to receive statutory adoption pay if—
-- src:3570 | (a) he has elected in accordance with section 171ZB above to receive statutory paternity pay, or
-- src:3571 | (b) he falls within subsection (4A).
@ref s 171ZL(4) (src:3569-3571)
GIVEN `he has elected in accordance with section 171ZB to receive statutory paternity pay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 171ZL(4A) he falls within the subsection` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(4) he may elect to receive statutory adoption pay` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `he has elected in accordance with section 171ZB to receive statutory paternity pay`
            THEN JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person may not elect to receive statutory adoption pay if— (a) he has elected in accordance with section 171ZB above to receive statutory paternity pay"
        IF `s 171ZL(4A) he falls within the subsection` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person may not elect to receive statutory adoption pay if— ... (b) he falls within subsection (4A)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection bars an election in two cases and does not itself grant it otherwise

-- Plain gloss: the entitlement is not changed by the placement of more than one child as part of
-- the same arrangement. For a placement under s 22C or s 81, the same is said of that placement
-- (subsections (9)(d) and (11)(d)).
-- src:3580 | (5) A person’s entitlement to statutory adoption pay shall not be affected by the placement, or expected placement, for adoption of more than one child as part of the same arrangement.
@ref s 171ZL(5) (src:3580)
-- src:3603 | (d) the reference in subsection (5) to placement, or expected placement, for adoption is to be treated as a reference to placement, or expected placement, under section 22C.
-- src:3609 | (d) the reference in subsection (5) to placement, or expected placement, for adoption is to be treated as a reference to placement, or expected placement under section 81.
@ref s 171ZL(5), s 171ZL(9)(d), s 171ZL(11)(d) (src:3580) (src:3603) (src:3609)
GIVEN `more than one child is placed, or expected to be placed, as part of the same arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(5) the entitlement is affected by the placement, or expected placement, of more than one child` MEANS
    IF `more than one child is placed, or expected to be placed, as part of the same arrangement`
    THEN JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person's entitlement to statutory adoption pay shall not be affected by the placement, or expected placement, for adoption of more than one child as part of the same arrangement."
    ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of more than one child

-- Plain gloss: notice. He is entitled to payments only if (a) he tells the person who will have to
-- pay the date from which he expects the liability to begin, and (b) he gives the notice at least 28 days
-- before that date or, if that is not reasonably practicable, as soon as is reasonably practicable.
-- src:3582 | (a) he gives the person who will be liable to pay it notice of the date from which he expects the liability to pay him statutory adoption pay to begin; and
@ref s 171ZL(6)(a) (src:3582)
GIVEN `he gives the person who will be liable to pay it notice of the date from which he expects the liability to pay him statutory adoption pay to begin` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(6)(a) he gives the notice of the date the liability is to begin` MEANS
    IF `he gives the person who will be liable to pay it notice of the date from which he expects the liability to pay him statutory adoption pay to begin`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person shall be entitled to payments of statutory adoption pay only if— (a) he gives the person who will be liable to pay it notice"

-- src:3583 | (b) the notice is given at least 28 days before that date or, if that is not reasonably practicable, as soon as is reasonably practicable.
@ref s 171ZL(6)(b) (src:3583)
GIVEN `the day on which the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `the date from which he expects the liability to pay him statutory adoption pay to begin` IS A DATE
      `it was not reasonably practicable to give the notice at least 28 days before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was given as soon as was reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(6)(b) the notice is given at least 28 days before that date or, if that is not reasonably practicable, as soon as is reasonably practicable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF ((Day `the date from which he expects the liability to pay him statutory adoption pay to begin`) MINUS (Day `the day on which the notice is given`))
               AT LEAST `s 171ZL(6)(b) the least number of days of notice before the liability begins`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it was not reasonably practicable to give the notice at least 28 days before that date` AND `the notice was given as soon as was reasonably practicable`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person shall be entitled to payments of statutory adoption pay only if— ... (b) the notice is given at least 28 days before that date or, if that is not reasonably practicable, as soon as is reasonably practicable"

-- src:3581 | (6) A person shall be entitled to payments of statutory adoption pay only if—
@ref s 171ZL(6) (src:3581)
GIVEN `paragraph (a) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(6) the notice condition for payments of statutory adoption pay is met` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person shall be entitled to payments of statutory adoption pay only if—"
    `s 171ZL(1) all of these answers hold` (LIST `paragraph (a) is satisfied`, `paragraph (b) is satisfied`)

-- Plain gloss: the notice must be in writing if the person who has to pay asks for that.
-- src:3584 | (7) The notice shall be in writing if the person who is liable to pay the statutory adoption pay so requests.
@ref s 171ZL(7) (src:3584)
GIVEN `the person who is liable to pay the statutory adoption pay requests it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(7) the notice shall be in writing` MEANS
    IF `the person who is liable to pay the statutory adoption pay requests it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice shall be in writing if the person who is liable to pay the statutory adoption pay so requests." (marginal reading (a): a failed "if" counts as the text's no)

-- Plain gloss: subsection (8) lists what regulations may do (modify conditions (b) to (d), disapply
-- or modify the notice rule, require evidence, count employment as continuous, aggregate earnings,
-- say how earnings are calculated, deal with elections). It is a power, not a rule about a person,
-- and is not encoded; where a rule's answer depends on what regulations do, it is an input.

-- Plain gloss: a child placed by a local authority in England under s 22C of the Children Act 1989,
-- or in Wales under s 81 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014, with a foster parent
-- approved as a prospective adopter, is treated in subsections (2)(a) and (4A)(a) as a child placed for
-- adoption. A placement of neither kind is outside the modification.
-- src:3599 | (9) This section has effect in a case involving a child who is, or is expected to be, placed under section 22C of the Children Act 1989 by a local authority in England with a local authority foster parent who has been approved as a prospective adopter with the following modifications—
-- src:3600 | (a) the references in subsections (2)(a) and (4A)(a) to a child being placed for adoption under the law of any part of the United Kingdom are to be treated as references to a child being placed under section 22C in that manner;
-- src:3605 | (11) This section has effect in a case involving a child who is, or is expected to be, placed under section 81 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014 by a local authority in Wales with a local authority foster parent who has been approved as a prospective adopter with the following modifications—
-- src:3606 | (a) the references in subsections (2)(a) and (4A)(a) to a child being placed for adoption under the law of any part of the United kingdom are to be treated as references to a child being placed under section 81 in that manner;
@ref s 171ZL(9), s 171ZL(11) (src:3599-3600) (src:3605-3606)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of placement`
      `the child was placed by a local authority with a local authority foster parent who has been approved as a prospective adopter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(9) the placement is one to which the conditions of subsection (2) are applied` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `placed for adoption under the law of a part of the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE        -- the unmodified case, subsection (2)(a)
    WHEN `placed under section 22C of the Children Act 1989` THEN
        IF `the child was placed by a local authority with a local authority foster parent who has been approved as a prospective adopter`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (9) applies "in a case involving a child who is, or is expected to be, placed under section 22C ... with a local authority foster parent who has been approved as a prospective adopter"
    WHEN `placed under section 81 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014` THEN
        IF `the child was placed by a local authority with a local authority foster parent who has been approved as a prospective adopter`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (11) applies "in a case involving a child who is, or is expected to be, placed under section 81 ... with a local authority foster parent who has been approved as a prospective adopter"

-- Plain gloss: a person who has become entitled through a s 22C placement (subsection (10)) or a
-- s 81 placement (subsection (12)) may not also become entitled as a result of the child being, or being expected to be, placed for adoption.
-- src:3604 | (10) Where, by virtue of subsection (9), a person becomes entitled to statutory adoption pay in respect of a child who is, or is expected to be, placed under section 22C of the Children Act 1989, the person may not become entitled to payments of statutory adoption pay as a result of the child being, or being expected to be, placed for adoption.
@ref s 171ZL(10) (src:3604)
GIVEN `by virtue of subsection (9) he has become entitled in respect of a child placed under section 22C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(10) he may become entitled as a result of the child being placed for adoption` MEANS
    IF `by virtue of subsection (9) he has become entitled in respect of a child placed under section 22C`
    THEN JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the person may not become entitled to payments of statutory adoption pay as a result of the child being, or being expected to be, placed for adoption"
    ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of a person entitled by virtue of subsection (9)

-- src:3610 | (12) Where, by virtue of subsection (11), a person becomes entitled to statutory adoption pay in respect of a child who is, or is expected to be, placed under section 81 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014, the person may not become entitled to payments of statutory adoption pay as a result of the child being, or being expected to be, placed for adoption.
@ref s 171ZL(12) (src:3610)
GIVEN `by virtue of subsection (11) he has become entitled in respect of a child placed under section 81` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZL(12) he may become entitled as a result of the child being placed for adoption` MEANS
    IF `by virtue of subsection (11) he has become entitled in respect of a child placed under section 81`
    THEN JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the person may not become entitled to payments of statutory adoption pay as a result of the child being, or being expected to be, placed for adoption"
    ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of a person entitled by virtue of subsection (11)

§§ `s 171ZM Liability to make payments`

-- Plain gloss: the person who must pay is any person of whom the entitled person has been an
-- employee in the way s 171ZL(2)(b) describes. The Act names nobody else here; regulations can put
-- the liability on the Board (subsection (3)), and must deal with a former employer who dismissed
-- the employee to avoid liability (subsection (2)).
-- src:3612 | (1) The liability to make payments of statutory adoption pay is a liability of any person of whom the person entitled to the payments has been an employee as mentioned in section 171ZL(2)(b) above.
@ref s 171ZM(1) (src:3612)
GIVEN `the entitled person has been an employee of the person as mentioned in section 171ZL(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZM(1) the liability to make payments of statutory adoption pay is the person's` MEANS
    IF `the entitled person has been an employee of the person as mentioned in section 171ZL(2)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names who is liable, and says nothing of anyone else; subsection (3) can make the Board liable

§§ `s 171ZN Rate and period of pay`

-- The longest the adoption pay period can be, and the weeks at the earnings-related rate.
-- src:3617 | (2) Statutory adoption pay shall be payable, subject to the provisions of this Part of this Act, in respect of each week during a prescribed period (“the adoption pay period”) of a duration not exceeding 52 weeks.
@ref s 171ZN(2) (src:3617)
`s 171ZN(2) the longest adoption pay period in weeks` MEANS 52

-- src:3629 | (a) at the earnings-related rate, in respect of the first 6 weeks in respect of which it is payable; and
@ref s 171ZN(2E)(a) (src:3629)
`s 171ZN(2E)(a) the number of weeks payable at the earnings-related rate` MEANS 6

-- src:3631 | (2F) The earnings-related rate is a weekly rate equivalent to 90 per cent of a person's normal weekly earnings for the period of 8 weeks ending with the week in which the person is notified that the person has been matched with a child for the purposes of adoption.
@ref s 171ZN(2F) (src:3631)
`s 171ZN(2F) the percentage of normal weekly earnings` MEANS 90%

-- Plain gloss: "week" in subsections (2) and (2E) is any period of seven days.
-- src:3638 | (7) In subsections (2) and (2E) above, “week” means any period of seven days.
@ref s 171ZN(7) (src:3638)
`s 171ZN(7) the week convention of subsections (2) and (2E)` MEANS `any period of 7 days`

-- Plain gloss: "week" in subsections (3), (5) and (6) of this section, and in s 171ZP(5), is a week
-- that starts on the day of the week the adoption pay period starts.
-- src:3639 | (8) In subsections (3), (5) and (6) above, “week” means a period of seven days beginning with the day of the week on which the adoption pay period begins.
@ref s 171ZN(8) (src:3639)
`s 171ZN(8) the week convention of subsections (3), (5) and (6)` MEANS `a period of 7 days beginning with the day on which a stated period begins`

-- src:3658 | (7) In subsection (5) above, “week” means a period of seven days beginning with the day of the week on which the adoption pay period begins.
@ref s 171ZP(7) (src:3658)
`s 171ZP(7) the week convention of subsection (5)` MEANS `a period of 7 days beginning with the day on which a stated period begins`

-- Plain gloss: the adoption pay period is a run of whole weeks, at most 52, starting on the day
-- regulations prescribe. The duration is prescribed too, so the caller supplies both (seam S29).
-- src:3617 | (2) Statutory adoption pay shall be payable, subject to the provisions of this Part of this Act, in respect of each week during a prescribed period (“the adoption pay period”) of a duration not exceeding 52 weeks.
@ref s 171ZN(2) (src:3617)
GIVEN `the first day of the adoption pay period` IS A DATE
      `the duration of the prescribed period in weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
`s 171ZN(2) the adoption pay period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the duration of the prescribed period in weeks` GREATER THAN `s 171ZN(2) the longest adoption pay period in weeks`
            THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of a duration not exceeding 52 weeks"
        IF `the duration of the prescribed period in weeks` AT MOST 0
            THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no period of a duration of no weeks
        OTHERWISE JUST (Period WITH
                            `the first day` IS `the first day of the adoption pay period`
                            `the last day` IS (`the first day of the adoption pay period` PLUS ((`the duration of the prescribed period in weeks` TIMES 7) MINUS 1)))

-- Plain gloss: regulations can shorten the adoption pay period for a person ("A"). The number of
-- weeks it is shortened to is prescribed (seam S28: ssc7 asks for it by this name). A shortened
-- period is shorter than the period it replaces.
-- src:3618 | (2A) Regulations may provide for the duration of the adoption pay period as it applies to a person (“A”) to be reduced, subject to prescribed restrictions and conditions.
@ref s 171ZN(2A) (src:3618)
GIVEN `the first day of the adoption pay period` IS A DATE
      `the duration of the prescribed period in weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `s 171ZN(2A) the number of weeks to which the adoption pay period has been reduced` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
`s 171ZN(2A) the adoption pay period as reduced` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 171ZN(2A) the number of weeks to which the adoption pay period has been reduced` AT MOST 0
            THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection does not say what a reduction to no weeks is
        IF `s 171ZN(2A) the number of weeks to which the adoption pay period has been reduced` LESS THAN `the duration of the prescribed period in weeks`
            THEN `s 171ZN(2) the adoption pay period` `the first day of the adoption pay period` `s 171ZN(2A) the number of weeks to which the adoption pay period has been reduced`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to be reduced"

-- Plain gloss: subsections (2B) to (2D) say what regulations under (2A) are to secure and may
-- prescribe (where the reduced period ends; what restrictions and conditions; revocation). They are
-- limits on a power to make regulations and are not encoded.

-- Plain gloss: the earnings-related rate is 90 per cent of his normal weekly earnings for the 8
-- weeks ending with the week in which he is told he has been matched with the child.
-- src:3631 | (2F) The earnings-related rate is a weekly rate equivalent to 90 per cent of a person's normal weekly earnings for the period of 8 weeks ending with the week in which the person is notified that the person has been matched with a child for the purposes of adoption.
@ref s 171ZN(2F) (src:3631)
GIVEN service IS A `Service for statutory pay`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZN(2F) the earnings-related rate in pounds` MEANS
    service's `normal weekly earnings in pounds over the period the section names`
        TIMES `s 171ZN(2F) the percentage of normal weekly earnings`

-- Plain gloss: for the first 6 weeks in which statutory adoption pay is payable he gets the
-- earnings-related rate; for the rest of the adoption pay period, the lower of that rate and the
-- weekly rate regulations prescribe. The week number counts the first week he is paid as week 1.
-- src:3628 | (2E) Statutory adoption pay shall be payable to a person—
-- src:3629 | (a) at the earnings-related rate, in respect of the first 6 weeks in respect of which it is payable; and
-- src:3630 | (b) at whichever is the lower of the earnings-related rate and such weekly rate as may be prescribed, in respect of the remaining portion of the adoption pay period.
@ref s 171ZN(2E) (src:3628-3630)
GIVEN `the number of the week for which statutory adoption pay is payable, counting the first such week as week 1` IS A NUMBER
      service IS A `Service for statutory pay`
      `s 171ZN(2E)(b) the weekly rate prescribed in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 171ZN(2E) the weekly rate of statutory adoption pay for the week in pounds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of the week for which statutory adoption pay is payable, counting the first such week as week 1` LESS THAN 1
            THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is no week before the first week in which it is payable
        IF `the number of the week for which statutory adoption pay is payable, counting the first such week as week 1` GREATER THAN `s 171ZN(2) the longest adoption pay period in weeks`
            THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rate is for weeks of "the adoption pay period", which does not exceed 52 weeks
        IF `the number of the week for which statutory adoption pay is payable, counting the first such week as week 1` AT MOST `s 171ZN(2E)(a) the number of weeks payable at the earnings-related rate`
            THEN JUST (`s 171ZN(2F) the earnings-related rate in pounds` service)
        OTHERWISE JUST (min (`s 171ZN(2F) the earnings-related rate in pounds` service) `s 171ZN(2E)(b) the weekly rate prescribed in pounds`)

-- Plain gloss: the weekly rate regulations prescribe for the later weeks must not be below the
-- weekly rate of statutory sick pay (s 157(1): the figure the Act states, £123.25; the caller
-- supplies it, because s 157 is in Part XI).
-- src:3632 | (2G) The weekly rate prescribed under subsection (2E)(b) must not be less than the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for the time being specified in section 157(1) or, if two or more such rates are for the time being so specified, the higher or highest of those rates.
@ref s 171ZN(2G) (src:3632)
GIVEN `s 171ZN(2E)(b) the weekly rate prescribed in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `s 157(1) the weekly rate of statutory sick pay specified in section 157(1) in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZN(2G) the weekly rate prescribed is not less than the weekly rate of statutory sick pay` MEANS
    IF `s 171ZN(2E)(b) the weekly rate prescribed in pounds` AT LEAST `s 157(1) the weekly rate of statutory sick pay specified in section 157(1) in pounds`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be less than the weekly rate of statutory sick pay"

-- Plain gloss: a person is not liable to pay statutory adoption pay for a week in which the other
-- works for him under a contract of service, except in prescribed cases; whether the contract
-- existed before the adoption pay period makes no difference (subsection (4): the second input is
-- deliberately unused).
-- src:3633 | (3) Except in such cases as may be prescribed, a person shall not be liable to pay statutory adoption pay to another in respect of any week during any part of which the other works under a contract of service with him.
-- src:3634 | (4) It is immaterial for the purposes of subsection (3) above whether the work referred to in that subsection is work under a contract of service which existed immediately before the adoption pay period or a contract of service which did not so exist.
@ref s 171ZN(3), (4) (src:3633-3634)
GIVEN `the other works under a contract of service with him during any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract of service existed immediately before the adoption pay period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is one prescribed under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZN(3) the person is liable to pay statutory adoption pay to the other in respect of the week` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the other works under a contract of service with him during any part of the week` AND `the case is one prescribed under subsection (3)`
            THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except in such cases as may be prescribed"
        IF `the other works under a contract of service with him during any part of the week`
            THEN JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person shall not be liable to pay statutory adoption pay to another in respect of any week during any part of which the other works under a contract of service with him". The second input is immaterial: "It is immaterial ... whether the work ... is work under a contract of service which existed immediately before the adoption pay period or ... which did not so exist."
        OTHERWISE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection bars liability for a week of work and does not itself say there is liability otherwise

-- Plain gloss: except in prescribed cases, statutory adoption pay is not payable for a week in
-- which he works for an employer who is not liable to pay him statutory adoption pay.
-- src:3635 | (5) Except in such cases as may be prescribed, statutory adoption pay shall not be payable to a person in respect of any week during any part of which he works for any employer who is not liable to pay him statutory adoption pay.
@ref s 171ZN(5) (src:3635)
GIVEN `during part of the week he works for an employer who is not liable to pay him statutory adoption pay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is one prescribed under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZN(5) statutory adoption pay is payable to him in respect of the week` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `during part of the week he works for an employer who is not liable to pay him statutory adoption pay` AND `the case is one prescribed under subsection (5)`
            THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except in such cases as may be prescribed"
        IF `during part of the week he works for an employer who is not liable to pay him statutory adoption pay`
            THEN JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "statutory adoption pay shall not be payable to a person in respect of any week during any part of which he works for any employer who is not liable to pay him statutory adoption pay"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection bars payment for such a week and does not itself say it is payable otherwise

-- Plain gloss: a daily rate, where one is needed, is one seventh of the weekly rate.
-- src:3637 | (6A) Where for any purpose of this Part of this Act or of regulations it is necessary to calculate the daily rate of statutory adoption pay, the amount payable by way of statutory adoption pay for any day shall be taken as one seventh of the weekly rate.
@ref s 171ZN(6A) (src:3637)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of statutory adoption pay in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZN(6A) the daily rate of statutory adoption pay in pounds` MEANS
    `the weekly rate of statutory adoption pay in pounds` DIVIDED BY 7

-- Plain gloss: the first day of the 7-day week, counted from the day the adoption pay period
-- begins, that a given day falls in (the "week" of subsections (3), (5) and (6), and of s 171ZP(5)).
-- src:3639 | (8) In subsections (3), (5) and (6) above, “week” means a period of seven days beginning with the day of the week on which the adoption pay period begins.
@ref s 171ZN(8) (src:3639)
-- src:3658 | (7) In subsection (5) above, “week” means a period of seven days beginning with the day of the week on which the adoption pay period begins.
@ref s 171ZN(8), s 171ZP(7) (src:3639) (src:3658)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the first day of the adoption pay period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 171ZN(8) the first day of the week of the adoption pay period containing the day` MEANS
    IF day LESS THAN `the first day of the adoption pay period`
    THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the weeks are counted from the day the adoption pay period begins
    ELSE JUST (day MINUS ((day MINUS `the first day of the adoption pay period`) MODULO 7))

-- Plain gloss: where pay is payable through a s 22C placement (subsection (9)) or a s 81
-- placement (subsection (10)), the reference in (2F) to being notified of a match is read as being
-- notified that a child is to be, or is expected to be, placed with him under that section.
-- src:3640 | (9) Where statutory adoption pay is payable to a person by virtue of section 171ZL(9), this section has effect as if the reference in subsection (2F) to the week in which the person is notified that he has been matched with a child for the purposes of adoption were a reference to the week in which the person is notified that a child is to be, or is expected to be, placed with him under section 22C of the Children Act 1989.
@ref s 171ZN(9) (src:3640)
-- src:3641 | (10) Where statutory adoption pay is payable to a person by virtue of section 171ZL(11), this section has effect as if the reference in subsection (2F) to the week in which the person is notified that he has been matched with a child for the purposes of adoption were a reference to the week in which the person is notified that a child is to be, or is expected to be, placed with him under section 81 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014.
@ref s 171ZN(9), s 171ZN(10) (src:3640) (src:3641)
GIVEN `statutory adoption pay is payable to him by virtue of section 171ZL(9)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `statutory adoption pay is payable to him by virtue of section 171ZL(11)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Kind of placement`
`s 171ZN(9) the placement that the notification in subsection (2F) is read as` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `statutory adoption pay is payable to him by virtue of section 171ZL(9)` AND `statutory adoption pay is payable to him by virtue of section 171ZL(11)`
            THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the two subsections each apply to a different placement and the text does not say what happens if both are claimed
        IF `statutory adoption pay is payable to him by virtue of section 171ZL(9)`
            THEN JUST `placed under section 22C of the Children Act 1989`
        IF `statutory adoption pay is payable to him by virtue of section 171ZL(11)`
            THEN JUST `placed under section 81 of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): neither subsection (9) nor (10) modifies the reading

§§ `s 171ZO Restrictions on contracting out`

-- Plain gloss: a contract term cannot take away or cut down statutory adoption pay, or make an
-- employee pay towards the employer's costs of it. "To the extent that it purports" limits the voidness.
-- src:3643 | (1) Any agreement shall be void to the extent that it purports—
-- src:3644 | (a) to exclude, limit or otherwise modify any provision of this Part of this Act, or
-- src:3645 | (b) to require an employee or former employee to contribute (whether directly or indirectly) towards any costs incurred by his employer or former employer under this Part of this Act.
@ref s 171ZO(1) (src:3643-3645)
GIVEN `the agreement purports to exclude, limit or otherwise modify a provision of Part 12ZB` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement purports to require an employee or former employee to contribute, directly or indirectly, towards costs incurred by his employer or former employer under Part 12ZB` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZO(1) the agreement is void to the extent that it purports` MEANS
    IF     `the agreement purports to exclude, limit or otherwise modify a provision of Part 12ZB`
        OR `the agreement purports to require an employee or former employee to contribute, directly or indirectly, towards costs incurred by his employer or former employer under Part 12ZB`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the extent that it purports"

-- src:3646 | (2) For the avoidance of doubt, any agreement between an employer and an employee authorising any deductions from statutory adoption pay which the employer is liable to pay to the employee in respect of any period shall not be void by virtue of subsection (1)(a) above if the employer—
-- src:3647 | (a) is authorised by that or another agreement to make the same deductions from any contractual remuneration which he is liable to pay in respect of the same period, or
-- src:3648 | (b) would be so authorised if he were liable to pay contractual remuneration in respect of that period.
@ref s 171ZO(2) (src:3646-3648)
GIVEN `the agreement authorises deductions from statutory adoption pay that the employer is liable to pay in respect of a period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is authorised by that or another agreement to make the same deductions from contractual remuneration he is liable to pay in respect of the same period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer would be so authorised if he were liable to pay contractual remuneration in respect of that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZO(2) the agreement is protected from being void by virtue of subsection (1)(a)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the agreement authorises deductions from statutory adoption pay that the employer is liable to pay in respect of a period`)
            THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of "any agreement ... authorising any deductions"
        IF    `the employer is authorised by that or another agreement to make the same deductions from contractual remuneration he is liable to pay in respect of the same period`
           OR `the employer would be so authorised if he were liable to pay contractual remuneration in respect of that period`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be void by virtue of subsection (1)(a) above if the employer" (marginal reading (a): a failed "if" counts as the text's no)

§§ `s 171ZP Relationship with benefits and other payments etc`

-- Plain gloss: a day in the adoption pay period is not counted as a day of incapacity for work for
-- incapacity benefit, except as regulations prescribe. (Subsections (2) and (3) are powers.)
-- src:3650 | (1) Except as may be prescribed, a day which falls within the adoption pay period shall not be treated as a day of incapacity for work for the purposes of determining, for this Act, whether it forms part of a period of incapacity for work for the purposes of incapacity benefit.
@ref s 171ZP(1) (src:3650)
GIVEN `the day falls within the adoption pay period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is one prescribed under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZP(1) the day is treated as a day of incapacity for work` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day falls within the adoption pay period` AND `the case is one prescribed under subsection (1)`
            THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except as may be prescribed"
        IF `the day falls within the adoption pay period`
            THEN JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a day which falls within the adoption pay period shall not be treated as a day of incapacity for work"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of a day within the adoption pay period

-- Plain gloss: being entitled to statutory adoption pay does not take away or change what he is
-- owed under his contract of service. Subsections (5) and (6) then say how the two are credited.
-- src:3653 | (4) Subject to subsections (5) and (6) below, any entitlement to statutory adoption pay shall not affect any right of a person in relation to remuneration under any contract of service (“contractual remuneration”).
@ref s 171ZP(4) (src:3653)
GIVEN `he is entitled to statutory adoption pay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZP(4) the entitlement to statutory adoption pay affects his right to contractual remuneration` MEANS
    IF `he is entitled to statutory adoption pay`
    THEN JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any entitlement to statutory adoption pay shall not affect any right of a person in relation to remuneration under any contract of service" (subject to subsections (5) and (6), which credit one against the other)
    ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of a person entitled to statutory adoption pay

-- Plain gloss: contractual pay the employer has paid for a week of the adoption pay period counts
-- towards the statutory adoption pay it owes for that week, pound for pound (fork F-credit), so the
-- amount still owed is the liability less what was paid, and never less than nothing.
-- src:3655 | (a) any contractual remuneration paid to a person by an employer of his in respect of a week in the adoption pay period shall go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay statutory adoption pay to him in respect of that week; and
@ref s 171ZP(5)(a) (src:3655)
GIVEN `the employer's liability to pay statutory adoption pay for the week, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the contractual remuneration paid to him by the employer in respect of the week, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZP(5)(a) the statutory adoption pay still owed for the week in pounds` MEANS
    max 0 (`the employer's liability to pay statutory adoption pay for the week, in pounds` MINUS `the contractual remuneration paid to him by the employer in respect of the week, in pounds`)

-- Plain gloss: statutory adoption pay paid for a week counts, in the same way, towards the
-- contractual pay the employer owes for that week.
-- src:3656 | (b) any statutory adoption pay paid by an employer to a person who is an employee of his in respect of a week in the adoption pay period shall go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay contractual remuneration to him in respect of that week.
@ref s 171ZP(5)(b) (src:3656)
GIVEN `the employer's liability to pay contractual remuneration for the week, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the statutory adoption pay paid to him by the employer in respect of the week, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZP(5)(b) the contractual remuneration still owed for the week in pounds` MEANS
    max 0 (`the employer's liability to pay contractual remuneration for the week, in pounds` MINUS `the statutory adoption pay paid to him by the employer in respect of the week, in pounds`)

§§ `s 171ZQ Crown employment-Part 12ZB`

-- Plain gloss: a person employed by or under the Crown is treated as any other employee.
-- src:3660 | The provisions of this Part of this Act apply in relation to persons employed by or under the Crown as they apply in relation to persons employed otherwise than by or under the Crown.
@ref s 171ZQ (src:3660)
GIVEN `the person is employed by or under the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZQ Part 12ZB applies to the person as it applies to persons employed otherwise than by or under the Crown` MEANS
    IF `the person is employed by or under the Crown`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section speaks only of persons employed by or under the Crown

§§ `s 171ZR Special classes of person`

-- Plain gloss: regulations can change Part 12ZB for a person employed on a ship, vessel, hovercraft
-- or aircraft, or outside Great Britain at a prescribed time, or in prescribed employment on the
-- continental shelf. Subsection (2) lists what those regulations may in particular provide, and is
-- not encoded. Seam S25 supplies the s 120(2) definition.
-- src:3662 | (1) The Secretary of State may with the concurrence of the Treasury make regulations modifying any provision of this Part of this Act in such manner as he thinks proper in its application to any person who is, has been or is to be—
-- src:3663 | (a) employed on board any ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft;
-- src:3664 | (b) outside Great Britain at any prescribed time or in any prescribed circumstances; or
-- src:3665 | (c) in prescribed employment in connection with continental shelf operations, as defined in section 120(2) above.
@ref s 171ZR(1) (src:3662-3665)
GIVEN `the person is employed on board a ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is outside Great Britain at a prescribed time or in prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 120(2) the employment is in connection with continental shelf operations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is prescribed employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZR(1) regulations may modify Part 12ZB in its application to the person` MEANS
    IF     `the person is employed on board a ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft`
        OR `the person is outside Great Britain at a prescribed time or in prescribed circumstances`
        OR (`the employment is prescribed employment` AND `s 120(2) the employment is in connection with continental shelf operations`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power reaches persons "employed on board any ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft", "outside Great Britain" or in "prescribed employment in connection with continental shelf operations"

§§ `s 171ZS Part 12ZB: supplementary`

-- Plain gloss: "adoption pay period" is the period s 171ZN(2) describes.
-- src:3673 | “adoption pay period” has the meaning given by section 171ZN(2) above;
@ref s 171ZS(1) "adoption pay period" (src:3673)
GIVEN `the first day of the adoption pay period` IS A DATE
      `the duration of the prescribed period in weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
`s 171ZS(1) the adoption pay period` MEANS
    `s 171ZN(2) the adoption pay period` `the first day of the adoption pay period` `the duration of the prescribed period in weeks`

-- Plain gloss: "the Board" is the Commissioners of Inland Revenue.
-- src:3674 | “the Board” means the Commissioners of Inland Revenue;
@ref s 171ZS(1) "the Board" (src:3674)
`s 171ZS(1) the Board` MEANS `the Commissioners of Inland Revenue`

-- Plain gloss: the "employer" of an employee is the person who, under s 6, has to pay secondary
-- Class 1 contributions on the employee's earnings, or who would have to but for the s 6(1)(b)
-- condition or because the employee is under 16. Whether s 6 makes someone liable is ssc1's answer.
-- src:3675 | “employer”, in relation to a person who is an employee, means a person who—
-- src:3676 | under section 6 above is liable to pay secondary Class 1 contributions in relation to any of the earnings of the person who is an employee; or
-- src:3677 | would be liable to pay such contributions but for—
-- src:3678 | the condition in section 6(1)(b), or
-- src:3679 | the employee being under the age of 16;
@ref s 171ZS(1) "employer" (src:3675-3679)
GIVEN `s 6 the person is liable to pay secondary Class 1 contributions in relation to any of the earnings of the person who is an employee` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person would be liable to pay such contributions but for the condition in section 6(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would be liable to pay such contributions but for the employee being under the age of 16` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 173(a) the person is under 16` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZS(1) the person is the employer in relation to the employee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 6 the person is liable to pay secondary Class 1 contributions in relation to any of the earnings of the person who is an employee` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person would be liable to pay such contributions but for the condition in section 6(1)(b)`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person would be liable to pay such contributions but for the employee being under the age of 16` AND (`s 173(a) the person is under 16` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`s 6 the person is liable to pay secondary Class 1 contributions in relation to any of the earnings of the person who is an employee` EQUALS NOTHING)
            THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether s 6 makes the person liable is ssc1's answer
        IF `the person would be liable to pay such contributions but for the employee being under the age of 16` AND (`s 173(a) the person is under 16` EQUALS NOTHING)
            THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the employee is under 16 is s 173(a)'s answer
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“employer”, in relation to a person who is an employee, means a person who"

-- Plain gloss: "local authority" and "local authority foster parent" have the meanings the Children
-- Act 1989 gives them (s 105(1) of that Act). That Act is not among the sources, so each is asked as a fact.
-- src:3680 | “local authority” has the same meaning as in the Children Act 1989 (see section 105(1) of that Act);
@ref s 171ZS(1) "local authority" (src:3680)
GIVEN `the body is a local authority within the meaning of the Children Act 1989 (section 105(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZS(1) the body is a local authority` MEANS
    `the body is a local authority within the meaning of the Children Act 1989 (section 105(1))`        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "has the same meaning as in the Children Act 1989"

-- src:3681 | “local authority foster parent” has the same meaning as in the Children Act 1989 (see section 105(1) of that Act);
@ref s 171ZS(1) "local authority foster parent" (src:3681)
GIVEN `the person is a local authority foster parent within the meaning of the Children Act 1989 (section 105(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZS(1) the person is a local authority foster parent` MEANS
    `the person is a local authority foster parent within the meaning of the Children Act 1989 (section 105(1))`        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "has the same meaning as in the Children Act 1989"

-- Plain gloss: "modifications" includes additions, omissions and amendments. It says "includes",
-- so another kind of change is not ruled out and is NOTHING.
DECLARE `s 171ZS(1) Kind of change` IS ONE OF
    `s 171ZS(1) an addition`
    `s 171ZS(1) an omission`
    `s 171ZS(1) an amendment`
    `s 171ZS(1) another kind of change`

-- src:3682 | “modifications” includes additions, omissions and amendments, and related expressions are to be read accordingly;
@ref s 171ZS(1) "modifications" (src:3682)
GIVEN change IS A `s 171ZS(1) Kind of change`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZS(1) the change is a modification` MEANS
    CONSIDER change
    WHEN `s 171ZS(1) an addition` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 171ZS(1) an omission` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 171ZS(1) an amendment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 171ZS(1) another kind of change` THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“modifications” includes additions, omissions and amendments, and related expressions are to be read accordingly"

-- Plain gloss: in Part 12ZB "prescribed" means prescribed by regulations.
-- src:3683 | “prescribed” means prescribed by regulations.
@ref s 171ZS(1) "prescribed" (src:3683)
GIVEN `it is prescribed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZS(1) the thing is prescribed` MEANS
    IF `it is prescribed by regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“prescribed” means prescribed by regulations"

-- Plain gloss: an "employee" is a person gainfully employed in Great Britain, under a contract of
-- service or in an office, with earnings (as Parts 1 to 5 use that word); but regulations (subsection
-- (3)) can exclude some such persons and include some others. The converter shows "..." and a blank
-- paragraph (b) (src:3685-3686): words and a limb repealed.
-- src:3684 | (2) In this Part of this Act, “employee” means a person who is—
-- src:3685 | (a) gainfully employed in Great Britain either under a contract of service or in an office (including elective office) with earnings (within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5 above); ...
-- src:3686 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:3687 | (3) Regulations may provide—
-- src:3688 | (a) for cases where a person who falls within the definition in subsection (2) above is not to be treated as an employee for the purposes of this Part of this Act, and
-- src:3689 | (b) for cases where a person who would not otherwise be an employee for the purposes of this Part of this Act is to be treated as an employee for those purposes.
@ref s 171ZS(2), (3) (src:3684-3689)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
      `the person is gainfully employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is carried on in the territorial waters adjacent to Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 172(a) a reference to Great Britain includes the place` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the employment is with earnings within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations provide that the person is not to be treated as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations provide that the person is to be treated as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZS(2) the person is an employee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `regulations provide that the person is not to be treated as an employee` AND `regulations provide that the person is to be treated as an employee`
            THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the two kinds of regulation cannot both apply to one person, and the text does not say which prevails
        IF `regulations provide that the person is to be treated as an employee`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `regulations provide that the person is not to be treated as an employee`
            THEN JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for cases where a person who falls within the definition in subsection (2) above is not to be treated as an employee for the purposes of this Part of this Act"
        OTHERWISE definition
    WHERE
        inGreatBritain MEANS
            IF employment's `carried on in Great Britain`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE IF `the work is carried on in the territorial waters adjacent to Great Britain`
                 THEN `s 172(a) a reference to Great Britain includes the place`
                 ELSE JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“employee” means a person who is gainfully employed in Great Britain" (work outside Great Britain and outside the adjacent waters)
        restOfDefinition MEANS
                `the person is gainfully employed`
            AND (employment's `held under a contract of service` OR employment's `held in an office`)
            AND `the employment is with earnings within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5`
        definition MEANS
            CONSIDER inGreatBritain
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                IF restOfDefinition
                THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the adjacent waters are in Great Britain is s 172(a)'s answer
                ELSE JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“employee” means a person who is gainfully employed in Great Britain" (a limb other than the place already fails)
            WHEN JUST inside THEN
                IF inside AND restOfDefinition
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“employee” means a person who is— (a) gainfully employed in Great Britain either under a contract of service or in an office (including elective office) with earnings"

-- Plain gloss: "week" in this Part, except ss 171ZN and 171ZP, is a period of 7 days beginning with
-- Sunday, or another period if regulations prescribe one for the case.
-- src:3693 | (5) In this Part, except sections 171ZN and 171ZP, “week” means a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or such other period as may be prescribed in relation to any particular case or class of cases.
@ref s 171ZS(5) (src:3693)
`s 171ZS(5) the week convention of Part 12ZB` MEANS `a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or another prescribed period`

-- src:3693 | (5) In this Part, except sections 171ZN and 171ZP, “week” means a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or such other period as may be prescribed in relation to any particular case or class of cases.
@ref s 171ZS(5) (src:3693)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `regulations prescribe another period in place of a week beginning with Sunday for the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 171ZS(5) the first day of the week containing the day` MEANS
    IF `regulations prescribe another period in place of a week beginning with Sunday for the case`
    THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "or such other period as may be prescribed"
    ELSE JUST (day MINUS ((Day day) MODULO 7))

-- Plain gloss: normal weekly earnings are the average weekly earnings paid to him, or for his
-- benefit, under the contract of service with the employer in question during the "relevant
-- period" (subsections (6) and (7)); in prescribed cases regulations calculate them instead (subsection (8)).
-- src:3694 | (6) For the purposes of this Part of this Act, a person’s normal weekly earnings shall, subject to subsection (8) below, be taken to be the average weekly earnings which in the relevant period have been paid to him or paid for his benefit under the contract of service with the employer in question.
-- src:3695 | (7) For the purposes of subsection (6) above, “earnings” and “relevant period” shall have the meanings given to them by regulations.
-- src:3696 | (8) In such cases as may be prescribed, a person’s normal weekly earnings shall be calculated in accordance with regulations.
@ref s 171ZS(6), (7), (8) (src:3694-3696)
GIVEN `the earnings paid to him or for his benefit under the contract of service with the employer in question in the relevant period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks in the relevant period` IS A NUMBER
      `the case is one in which regulations require his normal weekly earnings to be calculated in accordance with regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 171ZS(6) his normal weekly earnings in pounds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the case is one in which regulations require his normal weekly earnings to be calculated in accordance with regulations`
            THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "In such cases as may be prescribed, a person's normal weekly earnings shall be calculated in accordance with regulations"
        IF `the number of weeks in the relevant period` AT MOST 0
            THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "relevant period" has the meaning regulations give it; a period of no weeks has no average
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the earnings paid to him or for his benefit under the contract of service with the employer in question in the relevant period, in pounds` DIVIDED BY `the number of weeks in the relevant period`)
